@title Contact mirror under a coil: numbers either side of each contact symbol, poles stacked, spare contacts dim (1366x768)
@area Schematic
@sizes 1366x768
# The coil -K1 on page 2 shows its contacts as a mirror: `1 [symbol] 2` per pole for the three-pole main contact, `13 [symbol] 14`, `21 [symbol] 22`, a changeover with its two throws stacked, then the spare contacts the device has (contacts.* properties) dimmed. -K2 has a four-pole main contact. A double click on a row jumps to that contact; Alt+Left comes back.
open qa/fixtures/contact-mirror.kopercad
wait 30
key PageDown
wait 10
shot page-fitted
double_click 120 400
wait 30
shot jumped-to-the-contact-page
# The contact shows the page.column of its coil under its tag; a double click on it jumps back.
double_click 422 387
wait 30
shot jumped-from-the-contact-to-its-coil
key alt+Left
wait 30
shot back-at-the-contact
check_layout
